    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0749" n="741" xml:id="pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/815: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-10T18:00:00-05:00">December 10,
                            1941—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. Your 481, December 8, 6 p.m. Please inform Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek as
                    from the President that the President deeply appreciates the attitude of the
                    Generalissimo and of the Chinese Government as expressed by General Chiang to
                    you on December 8. State also that the suggestions made by General Chiang at
                    that time are receiving prompt attention and careful study.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d564-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d564-f1" n="31" xml:id="d564-f1-content">
                <p>In his telegram No. 492, December 13, 6 p.m., Ambassador Gauss reported to the
                    Department that “Generalissimo has been informed”. (740.0011 Pacific
                    War/1045)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
